// `x -= y` is the same arithmetic as `x = x - y`, and has to answer the same.
//
// It did not. Every binary operator goes through the guard that makes a NaN an
// error — docs/spec.md: "any arithmetic that would produce one is RT046" — and
// compound assignment had its own little arithmetic that went round it. So
// `inf - inf` was RT046 and `a -= inf` was a NaN, which then poisons every
// comparison it reaches, since a NaN is equal to nothing, including itself.
//
// The message names the base operator rather than the compound one, because
// `Infinity - Infinity` is the arithmetic that has no answer and is what the
// reader has to see.
let inf = 1e308 * 10
var a = inf
a -= inf
print("unreachable: ${a}")
